 RATES PURSUANT TO THE ADVICE NOTICE                     )
 NO. 317


               ORDER GRANTING APPEARANCE PRO HAC VICE

      THIS MATTER comes upon Counsel’s Motion for Admission of Robert Rigonan

to Appear Pro Hac Vice for Coalition of Clean Affordable Energy (CCAE), filed on June

11, 2026.

The Hearing Examiners FIND and CONCLUDE:

      1.      The Motion requests that Robert Rigonan be admitted to appear before the

Commission pro hac vice as counsel for CCAE in association with local counsel Cara

Lynch. The Motion is unopposed.

      2.      The Declaration of Mr. Rigonan attached to the Motion shows that he is a

licensed attorney in good standing in the State of Colorado. The Registration Certificate

attached to the Motion shows that Mr. Rigonan has complied with Rule 24-106 NMRA by

filing the requisite Registration Certificate of Non-Admitted Lawyer with the State Bar of

New Mexico.

      IT IS THEREFORE ORDERED:

      The Motion for Admission of Rober Rigonan to appear in this proceeding pro hac

vice is GRANTED.
                  BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Order Granting Appearance Pro Hac Vice                       Docket No. 25-00082-UT


        ISSUED under the seal of the Commission at Santa Fe, New Mexico, on June 18,

2026.




